+# Secrets defined here are available for reference under env/secret (and registry/password)
+# in config/deploy.yml. All secrets should be pulled from the environment, a password manager,
+# or a file. DO NOT ENTER RAW CREDENTIALS HERE — this file is committed to git.
+#
+# Required secrets:
+#   SECRET_KEY_BASE  - Generate with: bin/rails secret
+#   SMTP_USERNAME    - Mail server username (leave unset for unauthenticated relays)
+#   SMTP_PASSWORD    - Mail server password (leave unset for unauthenticated relays)
+#
+# Optional secrets (for browser Web Push notifications):
+#   VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY
+#   VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY
+#   Generate with:
+#     bin/rails runner 'k = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{k.public_key}\nVAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{k.private_key}"'
+
+# Option 1: Read secrets from environment variables
+SECRET_KEY_BASE=$SECRET_KEY_BASE
+SMTP_USERNAME=$SMTP_USERNAME
+SMTP_PASSWORD=$SMTP_PASSWORD
+VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=$VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY
+VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=$VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY
+
+# Uncomment if using an authenticated external container registry in config/deploy.yml:
+# KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD
+
+# Option 2: Fetch secrets from a password manager (1Password, Bitwarden, AWS Secrets Manager, etc.)
+# See `bin/kamal secrets --help` for supported adapters.
+#
+# SECRETS=$(kamal secrets fetch --adapter 1password --account your-account --from Vault/Fizzy SECRET_KEY_BASE SMTP_USERNAME SMTP_PASSWORD VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY)
+# SECRET_KEY_BASE=$(kamal secrets extract SECRET_KEY_BASE $SECRETS)
+# SMTP_USERNAME=$(kamal secrets extract SMTP_USERNAME $SECRETS)
+# SMTP_PASSWORD=$(kamal secrets extract SMTP_PASSWORD $SECRETS)
+# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=$(kamal secrets extract VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY $SECRETS)
+# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=$(kamal secrets extract VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY $SECRETS)
